# TVM — Time Value of Money (HP-style solver)
#
# Global labels appear as the top shift row (F1..F5). Key a value, then press
# its label to store it; press FV to compute:
#
#   value  F1  -> N     number of periods
#   value  F2  -> I     interest rate, % per period
#   value  F3  -> PV    present value
#   value  F4  -> PMT   payment per period (end of period)
#          F5  -> FV    future value  (shown, and left in X)
#
# FV = -( PV·(1+i)^N  +  PMT·((1+i)^N - 1)/i ),  i = I/100
# Registers: 01=N 02=I 03=PV 04=PMT · 05=i 06=g 07=scratch
#
# Example: 10 F1  5 F2  -1000 F3  0 F4  F5  ->  FV = 1628,8946

LBL "N"
STO 01
RTN

LBL "I"
STO 02
RTN

LBL "PV"
STO 03
RTN

LBL "PMT"
STO 04
RTN

LBL "FV"
# i = I / 100
RCL 02
100
/
STO 05
# g = (1 + i) ^ N
1
+
RCL 01
pow
STO 06
# term1 = PV * g
RCL 03
RCL 06
*
STO 07
# term2 = PMT * (g - 1) / i
RCL 06
1
-
RCL 05
/
RCL 04
*
# FV = -(term1 + term2)
RCL 07
+
chs
view
RTN
